roduced to Japan from China during the Song Dynasty between the Heian until the early Kamakura period."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-japanese-noodles"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_noodles"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Ramen","dish/ramen"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Alkaline noodles","ingredient/alkaline-noodles"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Youmian","ingredient/youmian"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a8/Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg/500px-Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg","w":500,"h":364,"by":"Kropsoq","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresh_ramen_noodle_001.jpg"}},"ingredient/seekh-kebab":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/seekh-kebab","n":"Seekh kebab","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Seekh kebab is a type of kebab from the Indian subcontinent. It is made with  Indian spices, spiced minced or ground meat, usually lamb, beef, or chicken, formed into cylinders on skewers and grilled. It is typically cooked on a mangal or barbecue, or in a tandoor. Seekh kebabs are prepared in homes and restaurants throughout the Indian subcontinent."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-seekh-kebab"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seekh_kebab"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Kashmiri cuisine","cuisine/kashmiri-cuisine",[["Wazwan","dish/wazwan"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Goshtaab","ingredient/goshtaab"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Rogan josh","ingredient/rogan-josh"],["Tabak maaz","ingredient/tabak-maaz"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0c/Pakistani_Food_Beef_Kabobs.jpg/